[{:db/id 17592186162089 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7a5359f-8967-570a-b634-daaee8dbc9c1" "question-237a5725-5a0e-5e90-89ea-d6700e3a977b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f7a5359f-8967-570a-b634-daaee8dbc9c1" :question/id #uuid "f7a5359f-8967-570a-b634-daaee8dbc9c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-138535" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & 0 & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dce23d7e-7b89-51d8-91ae-2e6f5b73477c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dce23d7e-7b89-51d8-91ae-2e6f5b73477c" :answer-field/id #uuid "dce23d7e-7b89-51d8-91ae-2e6f5b73477c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-96fb9c14-df10-5b90-9b22-46eaa98a547f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96fb9c14-df10-5b90-9b22-46eaa98a547f" "answer-299c3fa6-9fa8-5565-8634-09054fedc6f1" "answer-16d71454-0458-5173-92e2-d24ae7d33b2b" "answer-48db3d3c-30c7-55ab-a903-b5f38c30500f" "answer-f34f3108-25b4-52ad-8686-5c2f57c96aad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96fb9c14-df10-5b90-9b22-46eaa98a547f" :answer/id #uuid "96fb9c14-df10-5b90-9b22-46eaa98a547f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-299c3fa6-9fa8-5565-8634-09054fedc6f1" :answer/id #uuid "299c3fa6-9fa8-5565-8634-09054fedc6f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d71454-0458-5173-92e2-d24ae7d33b2b" :answer/id #uuid "16d71454-0458-5173-92e2-d24ae7d33b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48db3d3c-30c7-55ab-a903-b5f38c30500f" :answer/id #uuid "48db3d3c-30c7-55ab-a903-b5f38c30500f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f34f3108-25b4-52ad-8686-5c2f57c96aad" :answer/id #uuid "f34f3108-25b4-52ad-8686-5c2f57c96aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-237a5725-5a0e-5e90-89ea-d6700e3a977b" :question/id #uuid "237a5725-5a0e-5e90-89ea-d6700e3a977b" :question/math-academy-id "q-138563" :question/problem "$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-22532903-9de5-5ea6-88dc-56a50c21802f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-22532903-9de5-5ea6-88dc-56a50c21802f" :answer-field/id #uuid "22532903-9de5-5ea6-88dc-56a50c21802f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-890f27c1-0c91-5b46-9f4e-6f30606040c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1e09d3c-fdfb-5162-bbc7-9d78cc139800" "answer-579ce615-12df-5c19-81bd-6fbd6731105e" "answer-0755beb3-73a6-5399-8b09-ddef07ddf09d" "answer-32b39ef8-9dd6-57b9-ab9a-17113d1beb75" "answer-890f27c1-0c91-5b46-9f4e-6f30606040c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1e09d3c-fdfb-5162-bbc7-9d78cc139800" :answer/id #uuid "c1e09d3c-fdfb-5162-bbc7-9d78cc139800" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-579ce615-12df-5c19-81bd-6fbd6731105e" :answer/id #uuid "579ce615-12df-5c19-81bd-6fbd6731105e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0755beb3-73a6-5399-8b09-ddef07ddf09d" :answer/id #uuid "0755beb3-73a6-5399-8b09-ddef07ddf09d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32b39ef8-9dd6-57b9-ab9a-17113d1beb75" :answer/id #uuid "32b39ef8-9dd6-57b9-ab9a-17113d1beb75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-890f27c1-0c91-5b46-9f4e-6f30606040c1" :answer/id #uuid "890f27c1-0c91-5b46-9f4e-6f30606040c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{50}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162091 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83e058d9-31bd-5eef-83c8-b6f7c1427845" "question-a18b0561-3c55-5481-a95c-144e99d62fb8" "question-f2315875-6b0f-5492-8e9e-75741c68b770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83e058d9-31bd-5eef-83c8-b6f7c1427845" :question/id #uuid "83e058d9-31bd-5eef-83c8-b6f7c1427845" :question/math-academy-id "q-138579" :question/problem "$$\n{U}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{Σ}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}5\\end{aligned}],\\,{V}_{r}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}],\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3fa58d8-221b-5878-a7cd-de5fff20b644"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3fa58d8-221b-5878-a7cd-de5fff20b